{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added an explicit `sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 2.5)` prior before `sigma_y` is used in the likelihood. This matches the existing finite bounds on `sigma_y` and makes the implicit proper bounded-uniform prior explicit for SafeStan's unique-prior requirement. No data changes were required. `N` is a size and `movie` is an index/predictor, so they are not protected.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int N;
  vector[N] y;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=2> movie;
}
parameters {
  vector<lower=0, upper=5>[2] theta;
  real<lower=0, upper=2.5> sigma_y;
}
model {
  theta ~ normal(3, 1);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 2.5);
  y ~ normal(theta[movie], sigma_y);
  /* equivalently:
    for (j in 1:2){
      theta[j] ~ normal(3, 1);
    }
    for (n in 1:N){
      y[n] ~ normal(theta[movie[n]], sigma_y);
    }
  */
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":6,"movie":[2,2,2,2,2,1],"y":[6.0,5.0,3.0,5.0,5.0,4.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
